Give header constants internal linkage

With clang on MinGW, a namespace-scope inline variable gets its own
COMDAT .ctors entry, emitted before the translation unit's own
initializer; the MinGW CRT runs .ctors backwards, so ordinary globals of
the same TU (e.g. DEFAULT_AUDIO_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES in
audioengineconfiguration.cpp, which uses SOUNDFONT_NAME_ATTRIBUTE) are
constructed before the inline variables they read, and MuseScore crashed
in a static initializer before main().

Make these header constants 'static const': they are then part of each
TU's ordered dynamic initialization.

